# Section 6, ORS and SRS (the dialogs re-emitted by hand 2026-10-19, now generated; the examples as the
# peer lane committed them in 5f5cbce2 after the SRS sign fix, PLAN_CONSOLIDATION 1.2 (gg)).
# s06_ors_coro: CoroExample.in, the first near-field reference surface (element 5, PropType NF1) set 4%
#   long with MODify; ORS recovers the design 6.3293 (5 figures).
# s06_srs_coro: continuing, element 7 disturbed (f 7.0, z -7.0) and slaved to 5: f back to 6.3293, z
#   NEGATIVE.  The prose after it, pinned below: INT 7 then agrees with the design deck's INT 7 to 5 figures
#   (peak 1.3052e-5; 1.3052468e-5 against 1.3052664e-5, 1.5e-5 relative), and slaving 5 to 7 returns z +6.3293.
# s06_ors_starved: a COPY of ImageDemo.in with its primary's tenth Zernike coefficient set to 5 mm (the
#   defect the PDF line wrap made, finding 1.2 (cc)); ORS names the starved trace and aborts.
# COPY: $ROOT/docs/macos-manual/examples/CoroExample.in s06
# COPY: $ROOT/docs/macos-manual/examples/ImageDemo.in s06
cd $TMP/s06
old CoroExample.in
# TRANSCRIPT: s06_ors_coro
mod
fElt(5)=6.6
q
ors
5
yes
# TRANSCRIPT: s06_srs_coro
mod
fElt(7)=7.0
q
mod
zElt(7)=-7.0
q
srs
7
5
yes
# TRANSCRIPT-OFF
int 7
/null
old CoroExample.in
int 7
srs
5
7
yes
! perl -i -pe 's/-3\.536721061D-05/5d0/' ImageDemo.in
old ImageDemo.in
# TRANSCRIPT: s06_ors_starved
ors
12
# TRANSCRIPT-OFF
